+# Mira clothing assembly v60 — preserved, not adopted
+
+This first assembled 3D candidate is saved for reuse and review. It **fails contact acceptance**: the new side-wrapping cape is still animated by the existing back-cape motion, causing new visible-surface intersections. The existing 8,000 triangle guard also fails for Mira. No guard was changed. The user's later instruction calls for much smaller image-defined parts before further assembly; work stopped at this preservation boundary. No NPC cape solver repair was started.
+
+Base `fc311bac0134b58e04891264c405bfd61eba22e3` contains deployed runtime `2bee64cff6482cb7770ba69e07673eefc8ad54ef`. Neither remote nor Site was changed. Actual whole-model WebGL comparison is unavailable (integrator reports GL Disabled). This is neither a rendered reference match nor a natural-clothing / PS4-quality result.
+
+## Reference and model scope
+
+Seven canonical generated multi-view files are identified by complete path, bytes and SHA256 in [garment provenance](../src/assets/characters/mira-garment-provenance.json). These are design references interpreted into authored control surfaces, not scans, CAD measurements or runtime texture images. Complete proportions, assembly neckline/waist, cape-v2 sides, hands cuffs and lower FRONT hardware set the priority. Rejected cape-v1 and the v2 swirly fabric motif are not adopted.
+
+The candidate replaces Mira's old torso/sleeves, short closed lower shell, chest bands/buttons/bar, belt and cuffs. It adds one integrated costume recipe: a sewn torso/armhole/sleeve surface, standing collar, folded shoulder cowl with two brooches, open split lower panels, fitted belt/buckle/hanger/tongue, and a longer cape wrapping the sides. It reuses the existing physical wool cache, leather and brass palette. No source image, new texture, animation, Game state or skeleton joint was added.
+
+Both armholes share 16 logical boundary vertices, common weights and normal accumulation with their sleeve lofts. The upper and lower ends overlap beneath a single belt line; the old separate short free hem is removed. The cape retains its row-major dynamic-surface contract (25 columns × 17 rows). This is a first shape interpretation, not proof that every generated silhouette or fold was reconstructed. Cowl/cape support, cuff layering, internal intersections, edge finish and reference-specific folds remain unresolved. Head/hair/hands/boots/staff keep the base model here; their separate candidates are not included and their match to the new reference is not claimed.
+
+## New native comparison
+
+The evidence's before actor/geometry files are exact copies of this worktree base, loaded through explicit Node module hooks. Six focused tests pass: sewn seam adjacency/weights; unchanged draw/bone allocation; all other 13 actor families exact in five shared API poses; preserved head/eye/hair/hand geometry; old lower-leg/foot and staff-bound vertices inside merged batches; independent cloned skeleton/cape/state with shared immutable skin geometry. The initial clone test failed because its same-material search selected the cape; the final predicate requires a skinned mesh. Both the raw failure and a compact explanation are retained, and that fixture fix changed no runtime source.
+
+| Measure | Base Mira | Candidate |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Visible triangles | 6,718 | 9,508 |
+| Visible material draws | 13 | 13 |
+| Bones | 41 | 41 |
+| Geometry attribute + index bytes | 319,180 | 412,584 |
+| Initial JS | 165,611 B | 165,611 B |
+| JS chunks | 3 | 3 |
+
+Candidate geometry has finite positions/normals/UVs and no zero-area triangles or zero-area UV triangles in the measured bind arrays. Weight sums differ from one by at most Float32 rounding (~3e-8). Signed UV winding includes intentional mirrored chart directions; zero negative winding is not claimed and no unique photographic atlas is applied. Physical UVs use length / 0.256 m, with shared existing cloth settings. Full deformed UV anisotropy / texture perception was not established by these tests.
+
+Seven poses (idle/walk/run/parry/attack/death 0.8/death 1 seconds) on flat and linear sloped ground sample seven points per visible triangle. New minimum floor penetration did not worsen in these 14 paired conditions. Existing stance/foot negative gaps on slopes remain (worst approximately −11.27 mm); contact sampling is not a continuous collision proof. Old NPC joint motion, first-seen/save behavior and Game implementation remain byte-identical. This unit does not claim a newly executed complete actual-Game lifecycle suite.
+
+The existing dialogue-framing oracle also passes its normal three viewport conditions using the actual main/Scene/Three matrices behind its declared Node renderer/asset/DOM mocks. It confirms framing and unobstructed existing eye targets; it does not draw the new costume or prove its visual match.
+
+## Required unresolved contact work
+
+A separate proper edge/triangle crossing oracle includes the complete visible wool and cape surfaces, with self tests. It excludes coplanar/boundary-only contact. The new topology means face/pair counts are diagnostics, not corresponding-face identities or exact penetration volumes.
+
+| Same pose | Old cape crossing faces | New cape crossing faces | Old / new total sampled crossing pairs |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| Idle | 0 | 129 | 450 / 1,273 |
+| Walk | 0 | 135 | 372 / 1,327 |
+| Parry API | 0 | 112 | 483 / 1,265 |
+| Raised-arm joint stress | 0 | 111 | 482 / 1,069 |
+| Death 0.8 s | 22 | 272 | 729 / 1,264 |
+
+New intersections include cape/sleeve, cape/leather, wool/skin and existing layered clothing contacts. Death includes 194 cape self-crossing pairs. The extended wrap requires a body-local NPC cape update and internal layer review; just shortening it to the old back-only shape would lose the approved reference. This is a known failure, even though sampled floor minima and other actors remain unchanged. No attempt to hide it behind aggregate area or more triangles was made.
+
+## Build, limits and handoff
+
+`node --test tests/mira-assembly.test.mjs`: 6 passed. Existing `tests/detailed-actors.test.mjs`: 5 passed / 1 failed at `npc triangle budget`; recipe and animation provenance tests passed. `npm run build`: success, 3.29 s reported by Vite; three chunks, initial 165,611 B, deferred scene 352,770 B. No media source changes. Full integration, package/artifact gate and device/GPU performance are not tested in this candidate. No performance conclusion follows from CPU construction or test timings.
+
+Implementation/reference-generation/validation/rework limits and completed tool sessions are recorded in `evidence/mira-assembly-v60/TIME.json`. The author performed no image generation. The next authorized work after preserving this candidate is a micro-part planning table outside the repo, not further large-part modeling. The integrator owns adoption, combined head/props budget, independent review and official display.
